# The drum's own colours, under the symbols.
#
# `face` is near white on purpose and not a taste decision: a texel MULTIPLIES
# the face's lit colour rather than replacing it (pse/texture.hpp), so the
# symbol's own colours only survive if what is under them is close to white.
# Paint the drum mid grey here and every symbol comes out muddy.
#
# Pure white, because the shading is what makes it read as a surface: the
# engine's lambert puts the payline face at 0.67 intensity, so a white drum
# renders as a mid grey cylinder and every symbol keeps two thirds of its own
# colour. Painting the drum grey here as well multiplies the two and every
# symbol comes out muddy.
newmtl face
Kd 1.000000 1.000000 1.000000

# The flat ends, which carry no symbol and want to read as the edge of a
# machined cylinder rather than as more of the printed face.
newmtl drum
Kd 0.451000 0.463000 0.510000
